 "python": "import math\ncarts = {}                                  # shared store, outside every server\nservers = [\"S1\", \"S2\", \"S3\", \"S4\"]\n\ndef handle(n, user, item):\n    server = servers[n % len(servers)]      # the load balancer picks any server\n    carts.setdefault(user, []).append(item)\n    print(f\"request {n} on {server}: {user} has {carts[user]}\")\n\nfor n, item in enumerate([\"ticket\", \"parking\", \"t-shirt\"]):\n    handle(n, \"ana\", item)\nprint(\"servers for 4,000 req/s:\", math.ceil(4000 / 1000))",
 "output": "request 0 on S1: ana has ['ticket']\nrequest 1 on S2: ana has ['ticket', 'parking']\nrequest 2 on S3: ana has ['ticket', 'parking', 't-shirt']\nservers for 4,000 req/s: 4",
